      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "import sys\n\n# Crucial: Allows Python to count digits of numbers this large\nsys.set_int_max_str_digits(200000)\n\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input())\n    \n    if n == 1:\n        print(1)  # Length of \"0\" is 1 digit\n        return\n\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n        \n    print(len(str(b)))\n\nsolve()\n",
      "statement": "Output the number of digits of the [[n]]th fibonacci number. The first fibonacci number is {{0}}, the second is {{1}}. The fibonacci sequence is where the next number is the sum of the first two numbers before it.",
